<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>net8.0;net9.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <RootNamespace>TechTeaStudio.Injector</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>TechTeaStudio.Injector</AssemblyName>
    <Version>0.4.0</Version>

    <Description>Lightweight, expression-tree-compiled dependency injection container for .NET 8/9/10. From-scratch with no Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection dependency. Open generics, decorators, Lazy/Func/Owned auto-resolution, lifecycle hooks (OnActivating / OnActivated), validate-on-build, async disposal, child scopes with extra registrations, modules, assembly scanning, keyed services, and IEnumerable / IReadOnlyDictionary collection injection.</Description>
    <PackageId>TechTeaStudio.Injector</PackageId>
    <PackageTags>di;dependency-injection;ioc;container;injector;open-generics;decorators;lifecycle-hooks;techteastudio</PackageTags>

    <GeneratePackageOnBuild>true</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CS1591</NoWarn>

    <!-- Turns on both the trimming (IL2xxx) and NativeAOT (IL3xxx) analyzers per-TFM so the
         library's own code is checked. The container is intentionally NOT trim/AOT-safe; the public
         entry points carry [RequiresDynamicCode]/[RequiresUnreferencedCode] so consumers get accurate
         diagnostics, and the analyzers below verify that annotation coverage stays complete. -->
    <IsAotCompatible>true</IsAotCompatible>

    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/TechTeaStudio/Injector</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>

    <PackageIcon>icon.png</PackageIcon>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>

    <PackageReleaseNotes>
v0.4.0: Engine hardening, faster resolution, and a richer resolution API.

Added:
  * Public keyed resolution: ResolveKeyed&lt;T&gt;(key), ResolveKeyed(Type, key), TryResolveKeyed&lt;T&gt;(key, out value) on IResolver.
  * Non-throwing resolution: TryResolve&lt;T&gt;(out value) and ResolveOptional&lt;T&gt;() (plus Type overloads).
  * Registration probe: IContainer.IsRegistered&lt;T&gt;() / IsRegistered(Type).
  * Open-generic decorators: RegisterDecorator on an open generic now wraps closed resolutions; decorators are pre-indexed by service type.
  * Non-public [Inject] methods are now invoked, matching property injection.

Fixed / changed:
  * Concurrency: _byServiceType is a ConcurrentDictionary, fixing a data race when open generics are closed under concurrent load.
  * Singletons are constructed exactly once under parallel resolution.
  * Lock-free activator caches plus a registration-lookup-before-collection fast path cut per-resolve overhead and lock contention.
  * Func&lt;T&gt; / Lazy&lt;T&gt; / Func&lt;P, T&gt; activators are cached (Func&lt;P, T&gt; no longer recompiles its expression per resolve).

For ASP.NET Core / Generic Host integration use the TechTeaStudio.Injector.Extensions.DependencyInjection sidecar package.

Full changelog: https://github.com/TechTeaStudio/Injector/blob/product/CHANGELOG.md
    </PackageReleaseNotes>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="..\..\icon.png"     Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
    <None Include="..\..\README.md"    Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
    <None Include="..\..\CHANGELOG.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
    <None Include="..\..\LICENSE.txt"  Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
